From ee1b0886137c9720989690732231ba0315cae093 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 22:08:22 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(memory):=20capture-on-exit=20=E2=80=94=20P?=
 =?UTF-8?q?reCompact/Stop=20hook=20+=20--session-summary?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Forge SessionStart INJECTS memory but nothing CAPTURES on the way out, so
long sessions lose learnings and memory stays orphaned (the eval scored
memory pull-only). Add the write half:

- New memory-capture CONTEXT intent in FORGE_HOOK_CONTRACT (schema 1.2.0);
  renderClaudeHooks emits PreCompact + Stop groups calling
  `forge hooks capture --harness claude --trigger precompact|stop`. The
  trigger rides as a CLI arg stamped by the event, so the CLI never reads
  hook stdin. Honest matrix: only Claude renders; cursor/codex/hermes carry
  a skip reason (SESSION_END_SUPPORT).
- `forge hooks capture`: persists a deterministic, token-bounded
  session-summary note (trigger + in-progress issues) to the memory store
  BEFORE context is compacted. FAIL-OPEN, emits no stdout (never injects
  into the turn, never drives the agent). Flood guards: a plain Stop with
  nothing in progress is a no-op, and a byte-identical repeat is deduped;
  PreCompact always records a boundary. The note omits a timestamp so
  identical session state dedupes cleanly (the store stamps its own).
- `forge remember --session-summary`: one-flag alias for
  --kind session-summary, the explicit agent-written path (reuses #392
  typed-notes --what/--why/--learned), surfaced via `forge memory add`.

Auto-capture is a deterministic safety-net, not an LLM summary; the rich
learnings capture is the explicit --session-summary path. Follow-up filed
under epic 0093a02a for prompting the agent to write learnings at exit
(PreCompact/Stop are trigger-only surfaces per the repo's verified matrix;
a Stop-block nudge would drive the agent — Usage Policy, kernel 6d10c1a1).

Kernel issue: 3867b9c2-17f8-4e34-9636-7870faeb5e59

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
